=pod

=head1 NAME

changetrack-ng.conf - configuration file for changetrack-ng

=head1 SYNOPSIS

F</etc/changetrack-ng/changetrack-ng.conf>

=head1 DESCRIPTION

B<changetrack-ng> reads an INI-format config file on every run.
Lines beginning with C<#> are comments; blank lines are ignored.
Key-value pairs use C<key = value> syntax.

The config may contain notifier credentials (for example in the OTLP notifier's
C<headers> key).  Set file permissions to C<0640> or stricter.

Scalar and array values support environment-variable expansion using
C<${VAR_NAME}>.  An undefined variable causes a startup parse error.

The C<HOSTNAME> token in values is replaced with the system's fully-qualified
hostname at parse time.

The file has three section types:

=over 4

=item B<[global]>

Runtime settings: VCS backend, paths, sensitive-file behavior, etc.

=item B<[notifier:I<type>:I<name>]>

Configures one notification instance.  I<type> is one of C<email>, C<webhook>,
C<otlp>, or C<file>.  I<name> is an arbitrary label (optional; blank defaults
to C<default>).  Multiple instances of the same type are supported.  Each
section must contain C<enabled = true|false>.  Disabled instances are discarded
at parse time.

=item B<[track]>

The list of files and directories to monitor.

=back

=head2 Drop-in directories

Three sibling directories adjacent to the main config file are scanned
automatically for additional C<*.conf> files (sorted order):

=over 4

=item F<conf.d/>   — C<[global]> sections only

=item F<track.d/>  — C<[track]> sections only

=item F<notifier.d/> — C<[notifier:*]> sections only

=back

Non-existent directories are silently skipped.

=head2 @include directives

  @include <path>
  @include-track <path>
  @include-notifier <path>

I<path> may be a file or a directory (directories scan C<*.conf> in sorted
order).  The C<-track> and C<-notifier> variants enforce section restrictions
in the included path.  A visited-paths guard prevents infinite recursion.
A missing path is a fatal parse error.

=head1 GLOBAL SETTINGS

=head2 Core

=over 4

=item B<vcs> = C<git> | C<rcs> | C<fossil> | C<svn> | C<hg>

VCS backend used to store change history.  Default: C<git>.

=item B<output_dir> = I<path>

Directory where VCS history is stored.  For whole-repo backends (git, fossil,
svn, hg) this is the root of a mirror tree.  For RCS, flat C<,v> files are
written here.  Default: C</var/lib/changetrack-ng>.

=item B<push_remote> = I<remote ...>

For whole-repo VCS backends: space-separated list of Git/SVN/etc. remotes to
push to after each commit.  Leave empty to skip push.

=back

=head2 Ignore patterns

=over 4

=item B<ignore> = I<pattern ...>

Additional glob patterns to skip during directory traversal, space-separated.
Added to the built-in defaults, which already exclude:

B<Editor temporaries:> C<*.swp> C<*~> C<#*#> C<.*.sw?> C<*.bak>

B<Archives:> C<*.gz> C<*.bz2> C<*.bzip2> C<*.xz> C<*.zst> C<*.7z>
C<*.zip> C<*.tar> C<*.tgz> C<*.tbz2> C<*.txz>

B<Package manager artifacts:> C<*.dpkg-*> C<*.rpmnew> C<*.rpmsave>
C<*.pacnew> C<*.pacorig>

B<Compiled bytecode:> C<*.pyc> C<*.pyo> C<*.elc>

B<System runtime:> C<mtab> C<ld.so.cache> C<prelink.cache> C<adjtime>
C<udev/hwdb.bin> C<lvm/cache> C<lvm/archive>

=back

=head2 Sensitive files

=over 4

=item B<sensitive_auto> = C<0> | C<1>

Auto-detect sensitive files by mode.  A file is treated as sensitive if it
has no group or world read bit (mode & 0044 == 0), e.g. mode C<0600>.
Default: C<1>.

=item B<sensitive_notify> = C<suppress> | C<allow>

How to handle sensitive-file diffs in outbound notifications.
C<suppress> replaces the diff with a placeholder; C<allow> sends the full
diff.  Default: C<suppress>.

Even when C<sensitive_notify = suppress>, notification payloads still include
the path of changed files.  This is an intentional auditability trade-off.

=back

=head2 Pre-commit checks

=over 4

=item B<warn_special_files> = C<0> | C<1>

Warn about special files (sockets, FIFOs, device nodes) and hardlinks.
Default: C<1>.

=back

=head2 Scheduling

=over 4

=item B<interval> = I<seconds>

Informational: used by C<make install-systemd> and C<make install-cron>.
Does not affect runtime behavior.  Default: C<3600> (one hour).

=back

=head2 Locking

=over 4

=item B<lock_path> = I<path>

Lock file path.  Default: C</var/run/changetrack-ng.lock>.

=item B<lock_timeout> = I<seconds>

Seconds to wait for the lock.  C<0> means skip silently if locked, which is
the cron-friendly default.  Default: C<0>.

=back

=head1 NOTIFIER SECTIONS

Each C<[notifier:I<type>:I<name>]> section configures one notification instance.
I<type> must be C<email>, C<webhook>, C<otlp>, or C<file>.  I<name> is an
arbitrary label; omitting it (C<[notifier:email]>) is equivalent to
C<[notifier:email:default]>.  Multiple instances of the same type are supported.
Duplicate C<type:name> combinations — within a file or across all loaded files —
are a fatal parse error.

Every notifier section must include:

  enabled = true | false

Disabled instances (C<enabled = false>) are discarded at parse time and produce
no runtime object.

=head2 Common key

=over 4

=item B<sensitive_notify> = C<suppress> | C<allow>

Per-notifier override of the global C<sensitive_notify> setting.  When set,
takes precedence over the global value for this notifier instance only.

=back

=head2 Email notifier (type: email)

Pipes a plain-text diff report to C<sendmail>.

=over 4

=item B<to> = I<address ...>

Space-separated list of recipient addresses.  If omitted, recipients are taken
from the per-entry email lists in the C<[track]> section.  At least one
recipient must be resolvable at send time.

=item B<from> = I<address>

Envelope and header From address.  Supports C<HOSTNAME> token.
Default: C<changetrack-ng@HOSTNAME>.

=item B<sendmail_path> = I<path>

Path to the C<sendmail> binary.  Default: C</usr/sbin/sendmail>.

=back

=head2 HTTP Webhook notifier (type: webhook)

Posts a JSON payload to one or more HTTP(S) endpoints.

=over 4

=item B<url> = I<url ...>

Space-separated list of endpoint URLs.  Required.

=item B<full_diff> = C<0> | C<1>

Include full unified diff text in the payload.  Default: C<0>.

=item B<heartbeat> = C<0> | C<1>

Send a heartbeat payload even when no files changed.  Default: C<0>.

=item B<timeout> = I<seconds>

HTTP request timeout.  Default: C<10>.

=item B<insecure> = C<0> | C<1>

Disable TLS certificate verification.  Use only in controlled environments.
Default: C<0>.

=back

=head2 OTLP / OpenTelemetry notifier (type: otlp)

Exports one OTLP log record per changed file to an OpenTelemetry collector.

=over 4

=item B<endpoint> = I<url>

OTLP/HTTP endpoint URL (e.g. C<https://otelcol.example.com:4318/v1/logs>).
Required unless overridden by C<OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT> or
C<OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT>.

=item B<headers> = I<key=value ...>

Space-separated C<key=value> pairs sent as HTTP headers (e.g. for bearer token
authentication).  Treat this value as a secret; prefer injecting via
C<OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS> instead.

=item B<compression> = C<gzip> | C<none>

Payload compression.  Default: C<gzip>.

=item B<full_diff> = C<0> | C<1>

Include full unified diff text in log record attributes.  Default: C<0>.

=item B<heartbeat> = C<0> | C<1>

Emit a heartbeat log record even when no files changed.  Default: C<1>.

=item B<timeout> = I<seconds>

HTTP request timeout.  Default: C<10>.

=item B<insecure> = C<0> | C<1>

Disable TLS certificate verification.  Default: C<0>.

=item B<resource_attributes> = I<key=value ...>

Space-separated C<key=value> pairs added as OTLP resource attributes.

=back

=head2 File log notifier (type: file)

Appends one JSON object per run to a local log file.

=over 4

=item B<path> = I<path>

Path to the log file.  Required.

=item B<heartbeat> = C<0> | C<1>

Append a heartbeat record even when no files changed.  Default: C<0>.

=item B<full_diff> = C<0> | C<1>

Include full unified diff text in the JSON record.  Default: C<0>.

=back

=head2 Example

  [notifier:email:default]
  enabled      = true
  to           = ops@example.com
  from         = changetrack-ng@${HOSTNAME}

  [notifier:webhook:ops]
  enabled      = true
  url          = https://hooks.example.com/changetrack
  full_diff    = 1

  [notifier:otlp:default]
  enabled      = true
  endpoint     = https://otelcol.example.com:4318/v1/logs
  compression  = gzip
  heartbeat    = 1

  [notifier:file:audit]
  enabled      = true
  path         = /var/log/changetrack-ng.jsonl

=head1 TRACK SECTION

The C<[track]> section lists files and directories to monitor, one per line.

=head2 File entry

  /path/to/file [: email@example.com ...] [option=value ...]

=head2 Directory entry

  DIRECTORY /path/to/dir [: email@example.com ...] [option=value ...]

Directories are scanned recursively.

=head2 Per-entry options

=over 4

=item B<sensitive=auto|yes|no>

Override the global sensitive-file detection for this entry.

=back

=head2 Examples

  [track]
  /etc/passwd : root@localhost
  /etc/hosts
  DIRECTORY /etc/nginx : admin@example.com
  DIRECTORY /etc/ssl/private sensitive=yes

=head1 ENVIRONMENT

=over 4

=item C<OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT>

Overrides the C<endpoint> key in any C<[notifier:otlp:*]> section when set.

=item C<OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT>

Overrides both C<OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT> and the C<endpoint> config key
for the logs signal specifically (highest precedence).

=back

=head1 FILES

=over 4

=item F</etc/changetrack-ng/changetrack-ng.conf>

Default config location.

=item F</usr/local/etc/changetrack-ng/changetrack-ng.conf>

Installed default config when built with C<PREFIX=/usr/local>.

=back

